1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,752
Today I'm delighted to be joined again by Eve from Club Madeira.

2
00:00:05,102 --> 00:00:06,614
Welcome back Eve!

3
00:00:07,564 --> 00:00:08,668
Happy to be here.

4
00:00:09,618 --> 00:00:13,866
So today I wanted to ask about how you market the Smart Catalogue.

5
00:00:14,216 --> 00:00:15,848
What's your marketing door?

6
00:00:16,798 --> 00:00:17,878
Marketing door?

7
00:00:18,228 --> 00:00:19,548
I'm not sure I follow.

8
00:00:20,498 --> 00:00:24,170
Yes, when I worked in marketing we had a marketing door.

9
00:00:24,520 --> 00:00:28,888
We knew who our customers were because they walked through the marketing door.

10
00:00:29,838 --> 00:00:32,214
That's not how marketing usually works.

11
00:00:32,564 --> 00:00:35,612
Did your marketing door say 'fish and chips' over it?

12
00:00:36,562 --> 00:00:37,234
No.

13
00:00:38,184 --> 00:00:39,288
Car dealership?

14
00:00:40,238 --> 00:00:40,886
Okay.

15
00:00:41,236 --> 00:00:44,092
So how do you do marketing at Club Madeira?

16
00:00:45,042 --> 00:00:48,762
Marketing is about identifying people who will buy your product.

17
00:00:49,112 --> 00:00:54,680
What do you do if the person who walks through your marketing door has no use-case for your product?

18
00:00:55,630 --> 00:00:59,830
Well, I have to sell them something because they came through my marketing door.

19
00:01:00,180 --> 00:01:03,252
I can just make up a new product that they might buy.

20
00:01:04,202 --> 00:01:07,970
Marketing is about identifying people who will buy your product.

21
00:01:08,320 --> 00:01:16,648
If you have to make up a new product to sell to the person who walked through your marketing door, they are -by definition- not in your market.

22
00:01:17,598 --> 00:01:23,526
So who is the market for the Smart Catalogue, and how do you identify them without a marketing door?

23
00:01:24,476 --> 00:01:27,884
Club Madeira operates in three distinct markets.

24
00:01:28,234 --> 00:01:30,394
Clubs, partners and merchants.

25
00:01:30,744 --> 00:01:32,184
Firstly, clubs.

26
00:01:33,134 --> 00:01:35,366
Sorry, why clubs specifically?

27
00:01:35,716 --> 00:01:39,580
Can I not just put a Smart Catalogue on any website?

28
00:01:40,530 --> 00:01:44,082
We are an affiliate marketing company that earns on commission.

29
00:01:44,432 --> 00:01:49,928
Affiliate commissions require high traffic as conversion rates are typically around one percent.

30
00:01:50,278 --> 00:01:54,334
Each Smart Catalogue costs around twenty dollars per month to maintain.

31
00:01:54,684 --> 00:02:02,772
So to have any hope of commercial viability a Smart Catalogue must be on a site with the potential for around twenty sales per month.

32
00:02:03,122 --> 00:02:06,314
At one percent conversion that's two thousand clicks.

33
00:02:06,664 --> 00:02:11,752
Handing out Smart Catalogues to sites without any audience is a loss-making exercise.

34
00:02:12,102 --> 00:02:21,102
Our market is specifically clubs and community groups that have an unmonetised audience and members that will buy because they know their club gets the commission.

35
00:02:21,452 --> 00:02:25,916
A member has a reason to purchase through the Smart Catalogue rather than Amazon.

36
00:02:26,266 --> 00:02:27,730
A customer does not.

37
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:32,808
But my customer is never going to have two thousand clicks per month.

38
00:02:33,158 --> 00:02:35,126
They don't even have a website yet.

39
00:02:36,076 --> 00:02:37,036
Are they a club?

40
00:02:37,386 --> 00:02:38,586
How many members?

41
00:02:39,536 --> 00:02:40,136
No.

42
00:02:40,486 --> 00:02:42,862
But they walked through the marketing door.

43
00:02:43,812 --> 00:02:51,276
Okay, but without an audience to monetise or any chance of generating that audience, they aren't a Smart Catalogue customer.

44
00:02:52,226 --> 00:02:54,722
You mentioned you had a market for partners.

45
00:02:55,072 --> 00:03:00,616
Can I be a partner so I can give away Smart Catalogues to people who don't have any traffic?

46
00:03:01,566 --> 00:03:08,982
No, because every time you deliberately created an unsuccessful catalogue it would damage Club Madeira's reputation.

47
00:03:09,332 --> 00:03:13,748
We'd need to charge you twenty dollars per website per month to break even.

48
00:03:14,098 --> 00:03:19,114
You'd need to charge twenty times the going rate of one pound just to cover costs.

49
00:03:19,464 --> 00:03:26,280
And the moment you set off building websites in competition with our actual partners, they would refuse to deal with us.

50
00:03:27,230 --> 00:03:28,838
But I can make websites.

51
00:03:29,188 --> 00:03:30,844
Why can't I be a partner?

52
00:03:31,794 --> 00:03:35,442
We are an affiliate marketing company that earns on commission.

53
00:03:35,792 --> 00:03:40,904
Affiliate commissions require high traffic as conversion rates are typically one percent.

54
00:03:41,254 --> 00:03:44,446
Partners are people that manage websites with an audience.

55
00:03:44,796 --> 00:03:51,204
They engage that audience with marketing, SEO and promotion and deliver ongoing technical support.

56
00:03:51,554 --> 00:03:55,154
Do you manage any websites with an unmonetised audience?

57
00:03:56,104 --> 00:03:57,304
No, but...

58
00:03:58,254 --> 00:04:03,534
Can you provide marketing, SEO and promotion and deliver ongoing technical support?

59
00:04:04,484 --> 00:04:06,860
No, but I can make websites.

60
00:04:07,810 --> 00:04:11,890
Anyone with one pound per month and an Ionos account can do that.

61
00:04:12,240 --> 00:04:16,320
The web agencies who will survive are those that drive engagement.

62
00:04:16,670 --> 00:04:20,222
And right now they are looking for ways to differentiate their offering, 

63
00:04:20,572 --> 00:04:24,028
for client retention, for billables and for recurring revenue.

64
00:04:24,378 --> 00:04:29,394
For a company in the actual partner market, the Smart Catalogue offers all of that.

65
00:04:30,344 --> 00:04:33,800
Okay, so I'm not in the target market to be a partner.

66
00:04:34,150 --> 00:04:37,174
But what about the guy who walked through my marketing door?

67
00:04:37,524 --> 00:04:39,300
He's giving me buying signals!

68
00:04:40,250 --> 00:04:43,778
Take him to someone who can offer proper partner services.

69
00:04:44,128 --> 00:04:48,088
Tell him to ask for a Smart Catalogue and ask them to contact us.

70
00:04:48,438 --> 00:04:53,430
You have just gained a partner who will now look to see where else they can place the Smart Catalogue.

71
00:04:53,780 --> 00:04:59,180
And with the partner's marketing, SEO and promotion that catalogue might eventually break even.

72
00:05:00,130 --> 00:05:04,786
What if I ignore all that and set up as a partner behind your back anyway?

73
00:05:05,736 --> 00:05:08,904
We'd have to wish you all the best in your future endeavours.

74
00:05:09,254 --> 00:05:11,990
Do you want to hear about the market for merchants?

75
00:05:12,940 --> 00:05:16,012
No, ten thousand products is unrealistic.

